SUMMARY:(390) Alma hides a mag 11.4 star (just outside the path)
DESCRIPTION:(390) Alma hides a magnitude 11.4 star\, seen from Bangalore.\n
 The predicted edge passes 9 km to the S\, so a miss is likely — but a ch
 ord from near the edge is the most valuable observation of all.\nClosest a
 pproach 22:34:58 IST\, give or take 2 s. The star is 27° up in the ENE ·
  dark sky.\nIt fades 3.4 magnitudes for up to 4.1 s on the centre line\, a
 nd the path is 26 km wide\, give or take 15 km.\nThe map\, the finder char
 t and the path as KML: https://occult.alokm.com/asteroid?e=2026-09-10-390-
 alma-580096
